<title>USA: Burnham files $200 mln debt, equity shelf.</title>
<headline>Burnham files $200 mln debt, equity shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Burnham Pacific Properties filed Friday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission to register a shelf offering of up to $200 million in debt securities, common stock, preferred shares and warrants.</p>
<p>When added with previously registered securities, the company's shelf offering totals $321.7 million.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the sale will be used to repay outstanding debt, expand current properties and acquire additional retail shopping centers.</p>
<p>No underwriters were named in the shelf offering.</p>
</text>
